I *finally* made it! Party baby! Whooohoow! Toss in those !oBooze!
I don't have much notes on the game, neither i had the dump patch
installed, I actually only have some notes from the last stats NH gave
me... But i'll try to reconstruct the story...
Well, I certainly tried a lot and I have the impression the RNG had a
bit of mercy for me... My last three characters where all quite good,
one being petrified about three levels before Medusa, one being
poisoned by Demogorgon, and the last one being this one.
Nothing actually happened at the start, I think i lost my doggy
somewhere at the start because i can't remember having one.
First event has to be the Mines. I just go in there first, a character
coming back out is worthy of continuing, a character don't coming out
was, well, not good enough :). Actually not much happened. Minetown
altar had wrong alignment. Mine End was wine cellar, as usually, but i
dropped down to the Gnome King before I had my luckstone. This was
quite a tense moment because i didn't really feel prepared for the
hordes of G warriors. I fought my way back up (luckily i wasn't too
far from the stairs), and got the luckstone. I tunnelled a way to the
open again, then I went down again, prepared to run when needed. It
wasn't really necessary. Everything went fine and I bashed Ruggo the
Gnome King to death with my gloved hands. The throne gave nothing but
a few more nasties, but I wasn't afraid anymore. Back up to minetown I
started ID'ing all my stuff with the help of the shopkeepers'
services. I know it's lame but hey, this is my YAFAP.
Mall didn't bring too much, Oracle was boring, Sokoban was boring,
giving me my third BoH or so... but I already had a "oR too so it
actually didn't matter. I didn't encounter Rats nor Kobolds. Next was
the Orc Cavern, where not much happened. Quite uneventful part of the
journey, I would say.
First thing I encountered was the portal to the Neutral Quest, and I
stayed far away of that one. I have a bad experience with those gas
spores... After that I found the Quest, which I didn't take for
obvious reasons. Then I found my first altar... finally. I stayed
quite a long time around there, discovering the other two Quests. To
my shame, I was killed in Chaos. Being surrounded with L's and
escaping just in time is nice, but on the other side of the portal
some V's had gathered... luckily I had a "oLS (well I had already two
by then...)
After a bit of lingering around the altar, gaining XL, I managed to
kill Nightmare and some time later I finished the Neutral Quest by
slaying the Beholder. I took none of their artifacts because I don't
need them and I don't trust carrying around stridentily aligned
artifacts. I left Vecna aside for now.
I'm looking at the special location spoiler and I notice I didn't
encounter a lot of things. No Rats, no Kobolds, no Storage Room (I
don't think I ever had that one...), no Big Room (never had that one
either), no Nymphs, no Guild. It's a pity, except for the nymphs.
Around here I encounterd a priest, and started donating money to get
my AC down.
Wyrm Caves were next. Not to hard, wearing my "oR. Encountered my
first Big Dragons in here and finished them all of by hand. Next was
Lost Tomb, which I don't even remember... couldn't have been too hard,
then.
I think I found my first WoW about now. I wished for MM and Gauntlets
of Power. This being my YAFAP, I still have a lot to learn, for
example the value at wich armour evaporates when enchanted. I think I
wished 5 times or so for GoP, because they all disappeared from
over-enchanting :s. Well the hard way still is the most entertaining
way to learn.
I didn't bother with Sam. I could have killed him perhaps, or at least
I could have escaped, but I simply wouldn't want to run the risk. I
heard all those horrible stories about this one... No thanks.
Spiders were, strangly enough, quite hard. I stayed on the stairs and
had to come up some times to regenerate. Anyway after a couple of
times like that I decided to do something else first and then come
back down here.
The Sunless Sea was boring(what's the deeper meaning of this one? I
mean, the 'meaning' of the mine is all the G's and the luckstone, the
'meaning' of Sokoban is the puzzle and the reward, the 'meaning' of
the Wyrm Caves is the loads of D's and w's... what's with this one?
just the water? There is water on Medusa, too...), the Temple of
Moloch was boring but yielded an altar and some potions of full
healing (and lots of + and $ which I didn't use anymore). Giant
Caverns were boring too, but I had some 'fun' (=trouble) with T's and
Olog-hai... But not too much. The throne gave me another wish, but I
forgot what i wished for... Probably GoP ;) or an extra Cloak of MR.
Done Medusa without much trouble, then the Castle... Not much of
trouble here, either. I did some polypiling but got nothing valuable
(some iron golems perhaps), and in the throne room i decided to start
playing a bit and had a lot of fun using my =oConflict combined with
my Cloak of Displacement... All the grenades flying around in
impossible directions, all the soldats picking up these grenades,
after wich "you see the soldier explode"... I like it :)
Anyway got the wand of wishing and went back up, towards the Quest.
Did it without too much trouble, and with the use of a !oFH and a
!oInvincibility. Fairly easy that way :) Went towards the spiders with
my new toy, the Eyes of the Overworld. Spiders went down quickly, but
I didn't encounter a lot of good things here... Some !oFH where the
best to find.
Down to Gehennom... First thing was Frankenstein, which was quite a
surprise because I never saw this level before. Anyway one zap from a
/oD took him and some other weirdos out. Next were the Demon
Princes... a real pain. I skipped Demogorgon and Juiblex and pehaps
some others until later, because I fell down through a trap door, or
they teleported to the stairs and then upward... And it proved to be
quite a mistake.
Vlad was easy, but on the top level it was tense with a Planetar being
summoned. Luckily the corridors are small in Vlad's tower and a
/oTeleport can help you a bit. Speaking of Teleport, i had TC (via my
XL) and Teleportitis, and this combination saved some time and some
lives. Anyway, the Planetar was killed and the 2 Olog-hai he summoned
were safely locked up in a box. Time for Vladdie... Once again too
easy. Went down and towards the Wizard. Not very smart of me... I
first should have mapped all the levels, then made a rush... But no, I
simply got up and finished him off. I went down and got to the
Sanctum. Had to search a bit to find my way in, this being the first
time and I being still a bit unspoiled. Killed the high priest and
Rodney who had appeared YA time next to me. Worked my way back up and
then... A combination of Demogorgon, some other demons and a double
troubled Rodney struck me. He stole the Eyes, but luckely I had
another source of MR (cloak). It still was a pain wandering around the
mazes, fighting off hordes of &, but finally I managed to kill both
Wizards and all of the Demon Princes. From then on the game was
upwards. I made antoher mistake by trying to nurse-dance on the way
up... Rodney was spawned, some time later an Archon was spawned... I
quickly made my way out of Sokoban and up to the Elemental Planes.
Earth was easy, but Rodney made some (double) trouble. Still it was
going farily good. Air was quite easy too, had to use the /oTeleport a
few times, but simply bashed most of the monsters out of the way. Fire
was easy at the start. Then an Archon came. Then another Archon came.
Then a Solar came... I quickly fought my way to the portal... Water
was an easy resting place, because I had genocided ;. Perhaps it
wasn't necessary, but I didn't have a "oMagical Breathing, so I played
safe.
Astral took a long time. First guess was the middle one, with Famine.
I Killed Famine every single time with /oDeath. It turned out to be
the Neutral altar. Back down, killed Famine with /oDeath. To the left.
Encountered Pestilence and the Lawful altar. Grrrr... back out, killed
Famine with /oDeath. To the right with Death. He wasn't half as creepy
as I thought. He only hit me once before I killed him. Finally I
arrived at the Chaotic altar et voila... Here I am at the Bar...

